<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Multer + OneDrive-as-CDN Demo</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 760px; margin: 40px auto; padding: 0 20px; color: #1a1a1a; }
    h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; border-bottom: 3px solid #E4002B; padding-bottom: 6px; margin-top: 48px; }
    .step { background: #f2f2f2; border-radius: 6px; padding: 14px 18px; margin: 16px 0; font-size: 0.92rem; }
    .step ol { margin: 8px 0 0 0; padding-left: 20px; }
    form { margin: 16px 0; }
    input[type=text], input[type=url] { width: 100%; padding: 8px; margin-bottom: 8px; box-sizing: border-box; }
    button { background: #E4002B; color: #fff; border: none; padding: 8px 16px; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; }
    button:hover { background: #c40025; }
    .error { color: #c40025; font-weight: bold; }
    .gallery { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 16px; margin-top: 16px; }
    .card { border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 6px; padding: 10px; width: 180px; }
    .card img { width: 100%; height: 120px; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 4px; background: #eee; }
    .card p { font-size: 0.8rem; margin: 6px 0 0 0; word-break: break-all; }
    .badge { display: inline-block; font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: bold; color: #fff; border-radius: 3px; padding: 2px 6px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .badge.local { background: #595959; }
    .badge.cdn { background: #E4002B; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Multer Upload vs. OneDrive-as-CDN</h1>
  <p>Two ways to end up with a file URL, side by side.</p>

  <h2>Part 1 — Ordinary Multer Upload (file lives on this server)</h2>
  <p>This is the normal <code>diskStorage</code> pattern — the file is saved into this server's own <code>uploads/</code> folder and served from here.</p>

  <% if (uploadError) { %><p class="error"><%= uploadError %></p><% } %>
  <form action="/upload" method="POST" enctype="multipart/form-data">
    <input type="file" name="file" accept="image/jpeg, image/png" required>
    <button type="submit">Upload to this server</button>
  </form>

  <div class="gallery">
    <% localFiles.forEach(f => { %>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge local">LOCAL</span>
        <img src="<%= f.url %>" alt="<%= f.name %>">
        <p><%= f.name %></p>
      </div>
    <% }) %>
  </div>

  <h2>Part 2 — OneDrive as a "CDN" (Option A: manual link)</h2>
  <div class="step">
    This app does <strong>not</strong> talk to OneDrive's API. You upload the file to OneDrive yourself, grab a link, and paste it below — the app only automates the URL conversion.
    <ol>
      <li>Upload the file to OneDrive (personal account) via the web or desktop app.</li>
      <li>Right-click the file &rarr; <strong>Embed</strong> &rarr; click <strong>Generate</strong>.</li>
      <li>Copy the generated link — it looks like
        <code>https://onedrive.live.com/embed?cid=...&amp;resid=...&amp;authkey=...</code>
      </li>
      <li>Paste it below. This app converts <code>embed</code> &rarr; <code>download</code> automatically to build a direct link.</li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <% if (linkError) { %><p class="error"><%= linkError %></p><% } %>
  <form action="/cdn-link" method="POST">
    <input type="text" name="label" placeholder="Label (e.g. profile-pic.png)">
    <input type="url" name="embedUrl" placeholder="Paste the OneDrive Embed link here" required>
    <button type="submit">Register CDN link</button>
  </form>

  <div class="gallery">
    <% cdnLinks.forEach(c => { %>
      <div class="card">
        <span class="badge cdn">ONEDRIVE</span>
        <img src="<%= c.direct %>" alt="<%= c.label %>">
        <p><strong><%= c.label %></strong></p>
        <p>Direct: <%= c.direct %></p>
      </div>
    <% }) %>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
